---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// Describes what the site actually does today, not a generic template --
// every third party named below was confirmed against the built output.
// Two of them are easy to miss: article photos are hotlinked from
// Wikimedia (so a visitor's IP reaches Wikimedia on any page showing a
// photo, without them clicking anything), and the fonts are self-hosted,
// so there is deliberately no Google Fonts entry here.
//
// Keep this in sync when the analytics setup changes -- the cookie
// section below describes Google Analytics running without a consent
// gate, which is the current state, not a permanent decision.
const LAST_UPDATED = '7 September 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Chessori"
  description="What Chessori collects, who it goes to, and how to opt out. Plain English, no boilerplate."
  activeContinent="privacy"
>
  <header class="section-head">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p>Last updated {LAST_UPDATED}</p>
  </header>

  <div class="policy">
    <p class="lede">
      Chessori is a small chess news site run on a non-profit basis. It doesn't sell anything, doesn't run ads, and
      has no accounts to sign up for. This page sets out the data that does get collected, who receives it, and how
      to stop it.
    </p>

    <h2>Who is responsible for this site</h2>
    <p>
      Chessori is a non-profit publication operated from Finland, and is the data controller for the purposes of
      the GDPR. For any question about this policy, or to exercise any of the rights listed below, use the
      <a href="/contact/">contact form</a> &mdash; it reaches the person who runs the site directly.
    </p>

    <h2>What gets collected</h2>

    <h3>Analytics</h3>
    <p>
      This site uses Google Analytics 4 to count visits and see which articles get read. It sets cookies in your
      browser and collects your IP address, approximate location, device and browser type, the pages you view, and
      the site you arrived from. This is used only to understand what's worth writing more of. It is never used to
      identify you personally, and it is never sold or shared with anyone beyond Google.
    </p>
    <p>
      Google acts as a processor for this data and may transfer it to the United States under the EU&ndash;US Data
      Privacy Framework. Google's own handling is governed by
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's privacy policy</a>, and
      how long the data is kept is set by the retention setting on the Analytics property. Chessori does not keep a
      separate copy.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      Analytics currently loads on page view rather than after a consent prompt, which is under review. If you'd
      rather not be counted, there's a switch under <a href="#opt-out">How to opt out</a> below that turns it off
      for good &mdash; it stops the script being loaded at all, rather than just discarding what it sends.
    </p>

    <h3>Article photos</h3>
    <p>
      Photos are not stored on this site. They're loaded directly from Wikimedia Commons, which means your browser
      requests them from Wikimedia and your IP address and browser type reach Wikimedia's servers on any page showing
      a photo &mdash; without you clicking anything. Wikimedia's handling is covered by the
      <a href="https://foundation.wikimedia.org/wiki/Policy:Privacy_policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
        >Wikimedia Foundation privacy policy</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h3>Hosting</h3>
    <p>
      The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub receives and logs the usual server request data, including IP
      addresses, as part of serving the pages. See
      <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
        >GitHub's privacy statement</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h3>The contact form</h3>
    <p>
      If &mdash; and only if &mdash; you submit the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>, the name (optional), email
      address, topic and message you type are sent through
      <a href="https://web3forms.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Web3Forms</a>, which forwards them to a
      private email inbox. That's used to reply to you and nothing else. Messages stay in that inbox until they're
      deleted; ask via the form and yours will be removed.
    </p>

    <h3>Your theme preference</h3>
    <p>
      Choosing light or dark mode saves a single value (<code>chessori-theme</code>) in your browser's local storage
      so the site remembers it next time. It never leaves your device, isn't a cookie, and isn't seen by anyone. It
      goes away if you clear your browser data.
    </p>

    <h2>What is not collected</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No accounts, logins or passwords &mdash; there's nothing to register for.</li>
      <li>No advertising or advertising trackers.</li>
      <li>No social media pixels or embedded trackers.</li>
      <li>No fonts loaded from third parties &mdash; they're served from this site, so nothing is sent to a font provider.</li>
      <li>No payment data of any kind.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Legal basis</h2>
    <p>
      Hosting logs and the contact form rest on legitimate interest &mdash; serving the site securely and answering
      people who write in. Analytics cookies require consent under the ePrivacy rules; see the note above about the
      current setup. The theme preference is strictly necessary for a setting you asked for.
    </p>

    <h2 id="opt-out">How to opt out</h2>
    <p>
      The switch below is the direct route: turn it off and this site stops loading Google Analytics for you
      entirely, so nothing is requested from Google and no data about your visit leaves this page.
    </p>

    <div class="optout" id="optout" hidden>
      <div class="optout-row">
        <span class="optout-label">Analytics in this browser</span>
        <button type="button" class="optout-btn" id="optoutBtn">Turn off</button>
      </div>
      <p class="optout-status" id="optoutStatus" role="status">Analytics is currently on.</p>
      <p class="optout-caveat">
        This preference is stored in this browser only, so you'd need to set it again on another device &mdash; and,
        awkwardly, clearing your browsing data also clears it.
      </p>
    </div>
    <noscript>
      <p class="note">
        You have JavaScript disabled, so Google Analytics isn't loading at all and there's nothing to opt out of.
      </p>
    </noscript>

    <p>These all work too, and don't depend on this site honouring anything:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Block or clear cookies for this site in your browser settings. Nothing here breaks if you do.</li>
      <li>
        Use a browser that blocks trackers by default &mdash; Brave, DuckDuckGo, or Firefox with Enhanced Tracking
        Protection set to Strict. These stop Analytics outright.
      </li>
      <li>
        On a desktop browser, install
        <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
          >Google's Analytics opt-out add-on</a
        >, which applies to every site using Analytics. There's no mobile version.
      </li>
      <li>
        Private browsing helps, but less than it looks: it clears the cookies afterwards rather than preventing the
        data being collected in the first place.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under the GDPR you can ask for a copy of your data, ask for it to be corrected or deleted, object to it being
      processed, or ask for processing to be restricted. Use the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a> and it will be
      handled without charge, normally within a month.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you aren't satisfied with the response, you can complain to the Finnish Data Protection Ombudsman
      (<a href="https://tietosuoja.fi/en/home" target="_blank" rel="noopener">tietosuoja.fi</a>), or to the data
      protection authority in your own EU country.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      This site is a general-audience chess publication. It isn't directed at children and doesn't knowingly collect
      data from them.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      Any change will be reflected here with a new date at the top. The analytics arrangement described above is
      being reviewed, and this page will be updated when it changes.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<script is:inline>
  // The opt-out control. The flag it writes is read by BaseLayout before
  // the Analytics script is injected, so opting out means the script is
  // never requested at all -- Google receives nothing, not even the IP
  // address a blocked-but-loaded script would still have leaked.
  //
  // Rendered hidden and revealed here rather than shown by default: with
  // JavaScript off, Analytics never loads in the first place, so a
  // visible control would be both dead and misleading. The <noscript>
  // block covers that case instead.
  (function () {
    var KEY = 'chessori-analytics-optout';
    var GA_ID = 'G-KY9DGJ4ZDQ';
    var box = document.getElementById('optout');
    var btn = document.getElementById('optoutBtn');
    var status = document.getElementById('optoutStatus');
    if (!box || !btn || !status) return;

    function readOptedOut() {
      try {
        return localStorage.getItem(KEY) === '1';
      } catch (e) {
        return null; // storage unavailable -- can't read or persist a choice
      }
    }

    function render(optedOut) {
      if (optedOut === null) {
        btn.hidden = true;
        status.textContent =
          "This browser is blocking site storage, so the preference can't be saved here. One of the options below will work instead.";
        return;
      }
      btn.textContent = optedOut ? 'Turn back on' : 'Turn off';
      status.textContent = optedOut
        ? 'Analytics is off. Nothing is being loaded from Google on any page you visit here.'
        : 'Analytics is currently on.';
    }

    btn.addEventListener('click', function () {
      var next = !readOptedOut();
      try {
        if (next) localStorage.setItem(KEY, '1');
        else localStorage.removeItem(KEY);
      } catch (e) {
        render(null);
        return;
      }
      // Analytics already loaded on this pageview if they're opting out
      // now; this is the documented kill switch for an in-flight tag, so
      // the choice takes effect immediately rather than on next
      // navigation. Turning it back on needs a reload to inject the
      // script, which the status text doesn't promise otherwise.
      window['ga-disable-' + GA_ID] = next;
      render(next);
    });

    render(readOptedOut());
    box.hidden = false;
  })();
</script>

<style>
  .section-head {
    padding: 34px 0 10px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .section-head h1 {
    margin: 0 0 6px;
    font-family: 'Fraunces', Georgia, serif;
    font-weight: 540;
    font-size: clamp(30px, 4.5vw, 44px);
  }
  .section-head p {
    margin: 0 0 20px;
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  /* Matches the article body's measure and rhythm -- this is a page to be
     read, not scanned, so it gets the same treatment as a story rather
     than the full page width. Left-aligned rather than centred, so the
     prose starts under the h1: .section-head spans the full width here
     (as on contact/archive), and centring the column instead would leave
     the heading stranded out to the left of its own body text. */
  .policy {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 30px 0 60px;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .policy .lede {
    font-size: 19px;
    line-height: 1.62;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 0 0 8px;
  }
  .policy h2 {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', Georgia, serif;
    font-weight: 540;
    font-size: 26px;
    margin: 1.7em 0 0.5em;
  }
  .policy h3 {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', Georgia, serif;
    font-weight: 520;
    font-size: 19px;
    margin: 1.4em 0 0.4em;
  }
  .policy p {
    margin: 0 0 1.1em;
  }
  .policy ul {
    margin: 0 0 1.1em;
    padding-left: 1.2em;
  }
  .policy li {
    margin-bottom: 0.4em;
  }
  .policy a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration-color: var(--rule);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .policy code {
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.88em;
    background: var(--paper-raised);
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border-radius: 2px;
  }
  .policy .note {
    padding: 12px 16px;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--brass);
    background: var(--paper-raised);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 15.5px;
  }

  /* The one interactive control on an otherwise static page -- given a
     surface and a border so it reads as something to operate rather than
     more prose to read past. */
  .optout {
    margin: 0 0 1.4em;
    padding: 16px 18px 14px;
    background: var(--paper-raised);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 3px;
  }
  .optout-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 16px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .optout-label {
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 11.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .optout-btn {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    padding: 7px 16px;
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--ink);
    border-radius: 3px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    transition: opacity 0.15s ease;
  }
  .optout-btn:hover {
    opacity: 0.82;
  }
  .policy .optout-status {
    margin: 12px 0 0;
    font-size: 15.5px;
  }
  .policy .optout-caveat {
    margin: 8px 0 0;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
</style>
